{
  "id": 464132217,
  "iid": 23923,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "MKA: Properly get M for the ICV from EAPOL",
  "description": "As IEEE Std 802.1X-2020 9.4.1 Message authentication notes, the\nICV is calculated over what is often referred to as \"the frame\"\nbut explicitly does not include any VLAN or other tags that might\nbe before the EAPOL Ethertype. So the proper thing is to get the\nEAPOL frame from the EAPOL dissector similar to what is done for\nEAPOL-KEY type packets.\n\nThe EAPOL dissector only adds the proto data once, so calculate\nthe ICV on the first pass and store it. (That costs a bit of memory\nbut saves on CPU.)\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-03-14T12:36:04.956Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-03-14T18:24:26.189Z",
